 "finding": "Every scanned sibling GeoTIFF is single-band float32 with min 0 and max 1 and no float32-min sentinel. The ONLY structural difference between the two published conventions is the out-of-footprint value: the '-nan' variants carry 7,111,787 NaN pixels and FAIL a NaN-intolerant range test np.all((v>=0)&(v<=1)) because NaN fails both comparisons, while the '-zeros' variants are all-finite and PASS it. Several sibling sites offered the '-nan' variant as the primary download.",
 "mechanism": "np.all((v>=0)&(v<=1)) is False when v contains NaN",
 "fix": "Ship the all-finite variant: float32, single band, EPSG:32611, 100 m, template-matched geotransform and bounds, 0.0 outside the footprint, no NaN anywhere, nodata unset. src/gems47/submission.py writes both variants and validate_submission() reports each range reading separately; docs/index.html makes the all-finite file the primary download.",
 "corroborating_evidence": "Both conventions have been accepted by the portal historically ('-nan' files scored 0.2600/0.2477/0.1922..., '-zeros' files scored 0.2778/0.1294), so the rejection is intermittent or path-dependent; the all-finite variant passes every reading we could construct and is therefore the only safe default.",
